{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Create the opsbot account and supporting SSH key configuration on node1 and node2.","status":"satisfied","summary":"opsbot exists on both nodes with the expected home and shell. Node1 holds the Ed25519 private key, and matching authorized_keys files with restrictive ownership and permissions were observed on both systems, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-33459d4471004243","cmd-a0e97a8362c347dc","cmd-9a403edb659a438e","cmd-98f037d548e843c1","cmd-fa7b4754d9734291","cmd-5ceff9f06e7c4c07"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Allow opsbot on node1 to run commands over SSH as opsbot on node2 using a key.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct SSH tests from node1 executed on node2 as UID/user opsbot. The same behavior succeeded after both nodes had restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-bbec2a19e886498d","cmd-fa7b4754d9734291","cmd-7b8847fcb36f449a"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Require key-based authentication for opsbot on both systems.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Effective per-user sshd policy on both nodes enables public-key authentication, disables password and keyboard-interactive authentication, and requires the publickey method. Direct tests showed key authentication succeeding and deliberately key-disabled attempts failing with “Permission denied (publickey)” on both nodes, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-33459d4471004243","cmd-a0e97a8362c347dc","cmd-a0c62dd542894c64","cmd-fa7b4754d9734291","cmd-5ceff9f06e7c4c07","cmd-7b8847fcb36f449a","cmd-b791402621074567"]}],"confidence":1.0,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Account, key, authorized_keys, sshd configuration, SELinux-label restoration, and sshd reload actions directly established the requested outcome. known_hosts additions were bounded functional-verification prerequisites, and both reboots served the mandatory restart protocol. No failed services, new listeners, temporary residue, or package damage was observed afterward; lifecycle differences are consistent with the required restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-33459d4471004243","cmd-a0e97a8362c347dc","cmd-bbec2a19e886498d","cmd-a0c62dd542894c64","cmd-16d6a9faa0404b96","cmd-e0364e91dc224bab","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged restart, changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, recovered sshd/account/key/policy state, and successful post-restart SSH behavior.","limitations":[]}
